WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:01.867
-Good evening.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:02.902
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.236
We hope you're
doing well tonight.

00:00:04.236 --> 00:00:06.272
Now, if you don't mind,
we're gonna get to the news.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.374
President Biden
was interviewed last night

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:10.777
by CNN anchor Jake Tapper

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:14.747
and not, as he was expecting,
Walter Cronkite.

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:18.017
"Ah, you must be
the new kid, huh?"

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:19.852
President Biden said
in a new interview

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:22.088
that he doesn't think that
Russian president Vladimir Putin

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.857
will actually use
nuclear weapons,

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:26.159
though I don't think
it was a good idea to add

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:27.694
[Imitating chicken clucking]

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.163
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.365
In the same interview,
President Biden said

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:35.234
he doesn't expect the U.S.
economy to enter a recession

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:38.438
but added that if there is one,
it will be "very slight."

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:43.142
You can watch the entire clip
in a GOP campaign ad in 2024.

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:44.510
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.478
Buckingham Palace
announced yesterday

00:00:46.478 --> 00:00:49.748
that King Charles's coronation
will take place next year

00:00:49.748 --> 00:00:51.417
and said that the event will be

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:54.587
"rooted in long-standing
traditions and pageantry."

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:57.356
You know, the things that drove
his son and daughter-in-law

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:58.925
completely out of the country.

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:00.426
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:04.230
The Senate recently held its
12th-annual bipartisan luncheon,

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.200
which featured more than
560 pounds of barbecue

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.036
and I'm guessing
at least 10 paramedics.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.905
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.339
According to the latest numbers,

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:16.142
the Netflix series "Monster:
The Jeffrey Dahmer Story"

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.611
has been viewed
more than 700 million hours

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:19.912
since its release.

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:23.516
So get ready for NBC's
newest series, "Chicago Dahmer."

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:26.485
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:28.721
That's right -- The
Jeffrey Dahmer Netflix series

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.790
has been viewed
more than 700 million hours.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.991
I guess because it was
slightly less horrifying

00:01:32.991 --> 00:01:36.095
than "The Great British
Baking Show's" Mexican Week.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.464
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:42.268
"This is too much for me.
Should we go back to Dahmer?"

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.604
And finally, a winner
was declared yesterday

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:47.540
for the annual
Fat Bear Week contest.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.110
Said the winner, "Wait, I
thought it was just Bear Week."

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.912
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.517
You guys, guess what that was.
That was the monologue.

00:01:58.517 --> 00:01:59.786
Let's move on.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.054
We got a great show
for you tonight.

